Am I paranoid or what? It seem to me that the more I play and the more
successful I get, the nastier nethack gets in terms of starting attributes
and items. Is there something in the code that causes the program to look up
your previous performances and give you lousy stuff if they are good?

I can remember when I was just starting out on this game when I regularly
seemed to start every game with rings of regeneration, conflict, invisibility,
or +3 damage. I used to get blessed potions of healing, of gain ability, of
restore attribute, or speed. I can recall expecting to get scrolls of identify,
of genocide, of teleport, of enchant weapon or enchant armour. I can also 
recall thinking that wizards _always_ got 18 intelligence because I _always_
got 18 intelligence when playing a wizard. Now it seems that I get intelligence
of 16, two useless rings (protection against shapechangers/detect unseen) 
potions of confusion/poison/paralysis/booze/detect food/etc and scrolls of
fire/amnesia/sleep/etc. I seem to get a lot less of them too. I NEVER seem to
get a useful wand at the start anymore. Also my starting luck seems to be very
low. Every time I meet a water demon (usually while trying to get rid of a
curse) they attack me - I used to _like_ water demons because they always gave
me wishes. I can never seem to find an altar and shops seem a lot more scarce
than they used to be, 

Is this all just me being paranoid or is the game really rigged to give you a
hard time after a while. I know a lot more than I used to, and can cope with
the handicap to some extent, but it is awfully hard to start as a wizard with
lousy attributes and useless items. If it gets much worse the game will stop
being fun.

